# An enemy who bleeds out is as dead as one cut down: a body, and out of play for good.
#
# There are two ways to die in a fight and only one of them used to leave a mark. Fighter.IsAlive is
# `CurrentHp > 0 && !IsHumorDepleted`; NpcEntity.IsAlive reads the hit points alone. So a fighter bled
# dry by BleedingEffect — which sets IsHumorDepleted once the humor queues go fully critical — was
# dead for exactly as long as the fight lasted, and alive again at full health the moment the Fighter
# wrapper was dropped.
#
# Nothing about that failed loudly. CheckFightEnd counted them dead and awarded the victory;
# OnFightCompleted then asked enemy.IsAlive, was told yes, and skipped them. No corpse, no
# RemoveNpcFromPlay, no DepartedNpcs entry — a fight won against somebody still standing in the room,
# who the next visit rebuilt from the seed anyway. FightModeAdapter.SettleEnemyDeaths is the fix, and
# the two assertions below are its two halves: a body left, and the person gone.
#
# `fight-deplete` is the humor counterpart of `fight-end`, and it exists for the same reason: the real
# route is a bleed out-lasting a dozen turns of drain against full queues, and which special effect a
# blow rolls is not something a script can ask for. It takes `enemies` rather than a name because a
# narration fight pulls in every nearby NPC with authority, and their names are generated content.
# `inspect npcs` reports archetype ids, which are not — which is what makes `brewer` assertable.
#
# The fight is entered by the attack verb (see cli/verb/attack/success.cli for the flag reasoning).
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Hall" --period dawn --observe-only brewer

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# The man is alive and in the scene before any of this.
inspect npcs
expect-state npcs brewer

strategy succeed
goal attack
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

wait mode Fighting 90

# Everyone on the enemy side bleeds out at once. Nobody's hit points move, so this is the whole of
# the difference from cli/system/fight_victory_narration.cli.
fight-deplete enemies

# Depletion ends the fight exactly as wounds do — CheckFightEnd has always honoured it.
wait mode LocationInteraction 90
advance 12 180

# Half one: the victory left a body. Before the fix the scene came back with none.
inspect pois
expect-state pois Corpse

# Half two: and the man is out of play, not merely off screen. This is the assertion that would
# still have failed if the corpse were spawned without RemoveNpcFromPlay behind it.
inspect npcs
expect-no-state npcs brewer

quit
